rightkit-file-watch adapts approach and code from the following MIT-licensed project.

fsearch (https://github.com/noahdunnagan/fsearch), by way of rightkit-fsindex
  Adapted: the FSEvents stream binding (src/native/macos.rs): the extern
  declarations, stream creation, serial dispatch queue and start/stop sequence,
  as carried in rightkit-fsindex src/backend/macos.rs. Changes: retain/release
  callbacks own the callback state instead of leaking it, raw flags are decoded
  without panicking, event ids and a volume UUID feed a resume cursor.
  No git or crates.io dependency on upstream; the code is owned here.

The FSEvents flag-to-event mapping follows notify 8.2.0 (src/fsevent.rs), which
is released under CC0 1.0 Universal and needs no notice; it is listed for
provenance only.

